      "frontend_label_en": "Read-plan block success",
      "note": "Production: batterylifepo4.yaml template text_sensor id read_plan_success (entity_category diagnostic, not internal, so it is currently visible in HA). Clustered reads (M5): published as '<cluster id>:<cluster revision>:<success sequence>' (e.g. 'A1:5:77') after every successful cluster read, even when no decoded value changed; the browser marks every read-plan block inside that cluster (geometry from the /settings/read-freshness clusters[] array, never a browser-side copy) as read. A cluster whose group latched into the legacy fallback publishes the per-block form '<block address>:<revision>:<success sequence>' instead. The sequence counts every success (cluster and fallback block alike), so a jump shows that SSE coalesced success events in transit (the browser then re-reads /settings/read-freshness). The browser also accepts the older '<block address>:<revision>' form. The browser consumes it only as block freshness: ingestPayload() dispatches it to readBlockSuccess() before any diagnostic recording. Never a user-facing parameter."
    },
