      "frontend_label_en": "Read pause reason",
      "note": "Production: batterylifepo4.yaml template text_sensor id read_pause_reason (entity_category diagnostic). Clustered-read plan M8: 'none', or the transaction that owns the RS485 bus and pauses every ordinary read -- 'register_write' (a generic write slot in SENDING/ACK_WAIT/READBACK_WAIT; WRITE_UNCERTAIN does not hold the bus), 'cellcount', 'topology_recovery' or 'passcode'. Plan M8.1: 'register_write' also covers an accepted write intent while the pre-write quiescence barrier drains the Modbus hub, before its write is queued (at most 3000 ms, then the write is refused), and (plan M8.2) the transport cleanup after a transaction phase ends, until the Modbus hub holds none of that phase's frames. Computed by jk_write_tx::bus_owner(), the same predicate the generated read servicer pauses on, and published on change (the 100 ms snapshot interval, and at once when an intent is accepted or ends). The web UI shows 'paused for write' from it and disables every OK; it never refreshes or freezes physical freshness. Read-only, never a Settings parameter."
    },
